--- !u!114 &409378481
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 409378480}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 307bdc2def54f3c4194990377b07f814, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::BestiaryUI
  bestiaryPanel: {fileID: 1706953657}
  creatureDatabase:
  - speciesID: 1
    unlockedByDefault: 0
    displayName: Clownfish
    zone: Sunlight Zone
    gameSprite: {fileID: 5199603553472913348, guid: 00234d28f388fef4782f251e9d47dbc2, type: 3}
    realPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 218a25ea2ac089d4a8a2a2038435c600, type: 3}
    description: "\tThe clownfish can be many different colours, depending on its
      species, including yellow, orange, red, and black. Most have white details.
      They are smaller fish, with the smallest around 7 to 8cm long and the longest
      17cm long. \n\tClownfish live in warm reef waters and lagoons, often among
      sea anemones. They feed on small invertebrates, algae, and scraps left by their
      anemone hosts."
    trivia: All clownfish are born male! When the dominant female of a group dies,
      the largest male will change its gender to become the new head female.
  - speciesID: 2
    unlockedByDefault: 0
    displayName: Yellowfin Tuna
    zone: Sunlight Zone
    gameSprite: {fileID: -3969123534542766366, guid: cdfc738385eec8d4b8046facc0993295, type: 3}
    realPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 74b5df77613d0594a997b580ff018abd, type: 3}
    description: "\tA large, fast-swimming fish with a dark blue back and bright
      yellow fins that can grow up to 2.4 meters long. \n\tThey live in warm tropical
      oceans, forming large groups called schools to hunt small fish, squid, and
      crustaceans."
    trivia: Female yellowfin tuna are extremely productive. During spawning season,
      a female can release 1 to 4 million eggs at a time and may spawn every few
      days.
  - speciesID: 3
    unlockedByDefault: 0
    displayName: Great White Shark
    zone: Sunlight Zone
    gameSprite: {fileID: 7822194218038531395, guid: 15139b70d26a23e4e9c6fdcf6db66e3c, type: 3}
    realPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 091b3a572a119174299b09a0b26f4a87, type: 3}
    description: "\tThis large apex predator has a grey, torpedo-shaped body with
      a white belly, growing between 4.5 and 6 meters long.\n\tIt lives in coastal
      and open ocean waters around the world, using its sharp teeth to hunt marine
      mammals like seals and sea lions."
    trivia: Great white sharks can lose and replace up to 30,000 teeth over their
      lifetime!
  - speciesID: 4
    unlockedByDefault: 0
    displayName: Box Jellyfish
    zone: Sunlight Zone
    gameSprite: {fileID: -4954241958379642600, guid: a3a7bd264bf996d429434bf5412cf292, type: 3}
    realPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f653722769393da4f9b182295ffca8db, type: 3}
    description: "\tA pale blue, see-through invertebrate with a cube-shaped body
      called a bell that measures 20 to 30 cm across. \n\tIt drifts in warm coastal
      waters, using long clusters of tentacles to catch small fish and shrimp."
    trivia: "\tThey are among the most venomous marine animals, capable of causing
      human heart failure and death within minutes."
  - speciesID: 5
    unlockedByDefault: 0
    displayName: Great Barracuda
    zone: Sunlight Zone
    gameSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5aaf7da92faf53d4ba1e87f80d3bc0ab, type: 3}
    realPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1fd47a34c74edbd4188ededf7d47927a, type: 3}
    description: "\tA sleek, silver fish with a pointed head and large, sharp teeth
      that grows from 60 to 100 cm long. It lives near shallow coral reefs and mangroves,
      hiding in place to ambush fast-moving prey."
    trivia: "\tGreat barracudas can swim at lightning-fast sprinting speeds of up
      to 36 mph (58 kph)."
  - speciesID: 6
    unlockedByDefault: 0
    displayName: Mahi-mahi
    zone: Sunlight Zone
    gameSprite: {fileID: -2107366027826395023, guid: baef397314f107e40a1d9f422d9a95f4, type: 3}
    realPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 3ab41901c56b9d54e96f988b9f05c59e, type: 3}
    description: "\tA long, fast-growing surface fish with a large forehead and bright
      skin that flashes green, blue, and gold. \n\tIt grows up to 1.5 meters long
      and lives in open tropical waters, hunting smaller baitfish near the surface."
    trivia: They reach adulthood in just four to five months, making them some of
      the fastest-growing fish in the sea.
  - speciesID: 7
    unlockedByDefault: 0
    displayName: Red Snapper
    zone: Sunlight Zone
    gameSprite: {fileID: 7861710721230747446, guid: 83cacdd37eff6db498f7704a9004fef3, type: 3}
    realPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 0b2f1ccdabb97cb4ab3d0b2521b6edd1, type: 3}
    description: "\tA brick-red reef fish with a deep body and strong jaws that grows
      around 60 cm long. \n\tThey live near rocky structures, shipwrecks, and the
      ocean floor, feeding on shrimp, crabs, and small fish."
    trivia: Red snapper can live for more than 50 years, with some specimens recorded
      up to 57 years old in the Gulf of Mexico.
  - speciesID: 8
    unlockedByDefault: 0
    displayName: Goliath Grouper
    zone: Sunlight Zone Boss
    gameSprite: {fileID: 9184319047618853238, guid: b7612752786936042b5f976fce6224c1, type: 3}
    realPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 65f21d2aa904f3a4d9be2ded4396072d, type: 3}
    description: "\tA massive, thick-bodied reef fish with a brownish-yellow color
      and dark spots that can grow over 2 meters long.\n\tIt lives quietly inside
      caves, shipwrecks, and mangroves, using its giant mouth to swallow fish and
      crustaceans whole."
    trivia: "Can exceed 2 meters in length and weigh over 300 kilograms, earning
      them the nickname \u201Cgentle giants\u201D."
  skillDatabase:
  - speciesID: 'skill_bioluminescent_flare '
    unlockedByDefault: 1
    displayName: Bioluminescent Flare
    zone: Active Skill
    gameSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1f61579d7e3fd51449324d56165681fe, type: 3}
    realPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 94e0457b080554d4096410d6abca2d94, type: 3}
    description: "\tBioluminescence is light produced by a chemical reaction within
      a living organism. Bioluminescence is a type of chemiluminescence, which is
      simply the term for a chemical reaction where light is produced.\n\tMost bioluminescent
      organisms are found in the ocean. These bioluminescent marine species include
      fish, bacteria, and jellies. Some bioluminescent organisms, including fireflies
      and fungi, are found on land."
    trivia: "\tBioluminescence is a \"cold light.\" Cold light means less than 20%
      of the light generates thermal radiation, or heat."
  - speciesID: 'skill_echolocation '
    unlockedByDefault: 1
    displayName: Echolocation
    zone: Active Skill
    gameSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 90d69f1c453c13a4a9703174f1dd8aea, type: 3}
    realPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c9d7ccf6f78d2d3428863610991d17cf, type: 3}
    description: Something about echolocation
    trivia: trivia
  - speciesID: 'skill_camouflage '
